    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="0760" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/8989b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d716-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-02-24T17:00:00-05:00">February 24, 1939—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. I would like to have your report as to what extent the French Government
                    consider that Franco will refrain from executions on the basis of reprisals.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d716-f1" n="39" type="source" xml:id="d716-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Ambassador in the
                    United Kingdom as telegram No. 145, February 24, 6 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
